  "title": "Subgroup formed by elements of order dividing n",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture\n\nSuppose $G$ is a finite group, and $n$ is a positive integer dividing $|G|$. Suppose that $G$ has exactly $n$ solutions to $x^{n} = 1$. Does it follow that these solutions form a subgroup of $G$?",
